<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Fine-tuning Setting</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fine-tune the pre-trained RoBERTa-Base model on the GLUE benchmark using the Hugging Face library<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://huggingface.co/transformers/model_doc/roberta.html" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/transformers/model_doc/roberta.html</a></span></span></span>. All tasks are trained for 30 epochs with a batch size of 16. Refer to Table <a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ D.2 Fine-tuning Setting ‣ Appendix D Experiment Details ‣ PRAC: Principal-Random Subspace for LLM Activation Compression and Memory-Efficient Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> for the specific hyperparameters employed for PRAC.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T8" class="ltx_table">
