<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Additional Result</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compatibility with Advanced Optimizers.</span> PRAC is orthogonal to optimizer choice. We integrate PRAC with memory-efficient optimizers Muon <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and Adam-mini <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>. As shown in Figure <a href="#A4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ D.3 Additional Result ‣ Appendix D Experiment Details ‣ PRAC: Principal-Random Subspace for LLM Activation Compression and Memory-Efficient Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Table <a href="#A4.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ D.3 Additional Result ‣ Appendix D Experiment Details ‣ PRAC: Principal-Random Subspace for LLM Activation Compression and Memory-Efficient Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, PRAC successfully reduces memory by an additional approximately 30% on top of these optimizers with negligible perplexity degradation, highlighting its versatility.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="A4.F6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.F6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
